              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <h2 class="mt-14 text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900">
            Static lift against total — 30 gpm, 1-1/2 inch, 40 ft
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            The share column is the useful one: past about 10 feet of lift, the pipe stops mattering.
          </p>

          <div class="mt-8 overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white shadow-sm">
            <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
              <thead>
                <tr class="border-b border-slate-200 text-slate-500 bg-slate-50">
                  <th class="py-3 px-5 font-semibold">Static lift</th>
                  <th class="py-3 px-5 font-semibold">Friction head</th>
                  <th class="py-3 px-5 font-semibold">TDH</th>
                  <th class="py-3 px-5 font-semibold">Static share</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody class="text-slate-700">
                {
                  liftTable.map((row, index) => (
                    <tr class={index === liftTable.length - 1 ? "" : "border-b border-slate-100"}>
                      <td class="py-3 px-5 font-semibold text-slate-900">{row.liftFt} ft</td>
                      <td class="py-3 px-5">{fmt(row.frictionFt, 2)} ft</td>
                      <td class="py-3 px-5">{fmt(row.tdh, 2)} ft</td>
                      <td class="py-3 px-5">{fmt(row.staticShare, 0)}%</td>
                    </tr>
                  ))
                }
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-slate-500">
            Sources &amp; standards: total dynamic head as defined in standard pump engineering practice;
            friction from the Hazen-Williams equation as used in <a
              class="underline hover:text-orange-600"
              href="https://codes.iccsafe.org/codes/i-codes"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener">IPC</a
            > Appendix E and <a class="underline hover:text-orange-600" href="https://www.aspe.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
              >ASPE</a
            > guidance; velocity head from V² ÷ 2g with g = 32.174 ft/s²; pipe dimensions from <a
              class="underline hover:text-orange-600"
              href="https://www.astm.org/"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener">ASTM</a
            > D1785 and B88, with every bore computed from outside diameter and wall thickness. Net positive
            suction head and cavitation are not modelled — match the manufacturer's curve.
          </p>
        </div>
